5. Experimental Design and Data Eligibility

5.1 Dataset classification

Datasets are classified by contamination category:

· C₀ — independent, no known overlap with training data;
· C₁ — locus overlap possible, dataset independent;
· C₂ — high probability of training inclusion;
· C₃ — listed among training sources.

Confirmatory Track-A inference is restricted to in-distribution data only. Datasets that appear in the training corpus are excluded from confirmatory hypothesis testing; using a developer benchmark to test developer claims is circular.

5.2 Track-B datasets

Three CRISPR perturbation resources form the Track-B evidence base: a FlowFISH enhancer screen, a genome-wide pooled CRISPRi screen, and a TAP-seq enhancer screen. All three are in a single leukaemia cell line. This fact caps what the programme can claim: H2b is untestable with the current evidence base, and the confirmatory H2a claim is a statement about within-line conditioning, not about biological transfer.

The pooled screen is designated the primary H1 dataset on power grounds; the FlowFISH screen, with a validated pair set of approximately sixty, is designated a consistency check. The two screens are not pooled as if they carried equal evidential weight, and any pooled analysis carries an explicit dataset indicator. The readout difference between the screens — bulk FlowFISH versus high-multiplicity pooled single-cell — is disclosed.

The high-multiplicity design of the pooled screen creates correlated structure among guides. The cluster definition is fixed in advance (by gene, enhancer, locus, or guide), and a locus-level re-clustering sensitivity analysis is reported. If the H1 conclusion reverses under re-clustering, the conclusion is reported as fragile.

A non-K562 perturbation resource is a hard gate for any H2b claim. A larger compendium is not automatically cleaner: its underlying perturbation training data must be re-audited for overlap with the model's training corpus before use.

5.3 Dataset harmonisation

Before joint analysis, a common estimand is defined for the Track-B resources: a distance window, a false-discovery-rate threshold, and an effect-size floor. Harmonisation is a prerequisite for pooling, not a post-hoc adjustment.

5.4 Audit gates

No analysis code is executed until the preregistration is deposited. Audit code for the provenance-primitive verification is exempt because it is itself part of the frozen protocol. The primitive audit is executed with a minimal public notebook so that any reader can reproduce it, and it tests both the strict-subset property and the metadata consistency of the returned object.

