Appendix C — Hypothesis and Decision-Rule Registry

C.1 H1 — Distance-dependent magnitude miscalibration

Decision set: \{\text{supported},\ \text{equivalent},\ \text{inconclusive}\}.

· Supported if the clustered bootstrap interval for \Delta\gamma_3 excludes zero and |\widehat{\Delta\gamma_3}|>\mathrm{MDE}.
· Equivalent if TOST rejects both one-sided nulls at \delta^{\mathrm{eq}}_{H1}.
· Inconclusive otherwise.

A non-significant contrast is never reported as falsification. H1 is framed as a replication-and-quantification hypothesis, not a discovery hypothesis: distal underprediction in this model family is documented in the independent benchmark literature, and the confirmatory contribution is the direct estimation of \Delta\gamma_3.

C.2 H2 — Cell-state conditioning, split

H2a (testable): matched within-K562 conditioning improves Track-B prediction relative to a matched control. Supported only if both direction and magnitude exceed the MDE.

H2b (untested): the gain generalises to a non-K562 state. Marked untested in every abstract, figure, and preregistration statement until a non-K562 perturbation resource of usable scale is secured. This is a gating requirement, not a caveat.

C.3 H3 — Modality provenance

Estimated separately for \Delta_{\mathrm{sup}} and \Delta_{\mathrm{exp}} with the monotonicity expectation of B.9. Conditioning mode is declared per hypothesis: under expression conditioning no track carries the observed label, so hypotheses tested under different conditioning modes are not combined without explicit disclosure.

C.4 H4 — Evidence-based prioritisation

Decision set: \{\text{superior},\ \text{equivalent},\ \text{inconclusive}\}.

· Superior if \Delta@k>0 beyond the MDE.
· Equivalent if TOST rejects both one-sided nulls at \delta^{\mathrm{eq}}_{H4}.
· Inconclusive otherwise.

A small-but-real effect is therefore not misreported as null.

C.5 Composite falsification

The framework's value is falsified if, on the primary dataset with the pair set held fixed, all three hold:

1. the evidence layer does not improve validation yield beyond \delta^{\mathrm{eq}}_{H4};
2. the provenance contrast is flat across the three imputation modes;
3. the distance interaction is explained by a single global calibration slope rather than a distance-dependent term.

Stated in the preregistration so that a null outcome is interpretable as a finding.

